share":null,"area_key":"season_domain","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_map","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_comparison_map"]}],"paragraphs":[{"id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_West_finding_text","finding":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_West_finding","source_id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook","area":"EMI zone West","area_key":"zone","status":"validated","relationship":"weak_signal","text":"The platform does not show a unique favoured category over EMI zone West under its applicable rule. EMI prints 25% / 30% / 45% (below / near / above). Over the whole zone (as digitized from the EMI figure), the platform area mean is 32% / 33% / 35%: no clear category in one source.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22"]},{"id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_North-central_finding_text","finding":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_North-central_finding","source_id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook","area":"EMI zone North-central","area_key":"zone","status":"validated","relationship":"weak_signal","text":"The platform does not show a unique favoured category over EMI zone North-central under its applicable rule. EMI prints 10% / 30% / 60% (below / near / above). Over the whole zone (as digitized from the EMI figure), the platform area mean is 26% / 35% / 39%: no clear category in one source.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22"]},{"id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_South-central_finding_text","finding":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_South-central_finding","source_id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook","area":"EMI zone South-central","area_key":"zone","status":"validated","relationship":"same_favoured_category","text":"Both outlooks favour wetter-than-normal conditions over EMI zone South-central. EMI prints 15% / 30% / 55% (below / near / above). Over the whole zone (as digitized from the EMI figure), the platform area mean is 22% / 33% / 45%: same category.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22"]},{"id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_Southeast_finding_text","finding":"emi_belg_2026_outlook_zone_Southeast_finding","source_id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook","area":"EMI zone Southeast","area_key":"zone","status":"validated","relationship":"same_favoured_category","text":"Both outlooks favour wetter-than-normal conditions over EMI zone Southeast. EMI prints 20% / 35% / 45% (below / near / above). Over the whole zone (as digitized from the EMI figure), the platform area mean is 20% / 32% / 48%: same category.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22"]},{"id":"emi_shared_limitation","finding":null,"source_id":"emi_belg_2026_outlook","area":null,"area_key":"zone","status":"validated","relationship":null,"text":"The EMI zones were digitized from the figure's fill colours and placed by fitting the country outline, so their boundaries are approximate; the figure states no reference period, so probability differences are not calculated.","evidence_ids":[]},{"id":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_all_ethiopia_finding_text","finding":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_all_ethiopia_finding","source_id":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall","area":"All Ethiopia","area_key":"all_ethiopia","status":"validated","relationship":"same_favoured_category","text":"The outlooks favour different categories over much of their shared displayed area in Ethiopia. ICPAC shows a favoured category on 89% of Ethiopia and no forecast category shown (the legend does not explain the grey areas) on 11%; where it shows one it favours above normal on 69%, most often at 40-50% and 33-40%. The platform favours above normal on 50% and below normal on 7% of Ethiopia. There is category agreement of 54.8% within the compared area, which covers 59% of the analysed national area; opposite categories (above vs below) on 11% of the compared area. ICPAC publishes only the favoured category and its probability interval, so probabilities are not differenced. The official outlook covers Mar 2026–May 2026 and the platform Feb 2026–May 2026 (Feb 2026 only in the platform), so this compares spatial tendencies, not probabilities for the same seasonal event.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_map","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_comparison_map"]},{"id":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_season_domain_finding_text","finding":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_season_domain_finding","source_id":"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall","area":"FMAM rainfall domain (FMAM >= 20% of annual and >= 100 mm)","area_key":"season_domain","status":"validated","relationship":"same_favoured_category","text":"The outlooks favour different categories over much of their shared displayed area in the FMAM rainfall domain (FMAM >= 20% of annual and >= 100 mm). ICPAC shows a favoured category on 100% of the FMAM rainfall domain (FMAM >= 20% of annual and >= 100 mm) and no forecast category shown (the legend does not explain the grey areas) on 0%; where it shows one it favours above normal on 67%, most often at 40-50% and 33-40%. The platform favours above normal on 64% and below normal on 1% of the FMAM rainfall domain (FMAM >= 20% of annual and >= 100 mm). There is category agreement of 55.0% within the compared area, which covers 72% of the analysed domain; opposite categories (above vs below) on 9% of the compared area. ICPAC publishes only the favoured category and its probability interval, so probabilities are not differenced. The official outlook covers Mar 2026–May 2026 and the platform Feb 2026–May 2026 (Feb 2026 only in the platform), so this compares spatial tendencies, not probabilities for the same seasonal event.","evidence_ids":["platform_forecast_fmam","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_map","icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_comparison_map"]},{"id":"not_calculated","finding":null,"source_id":null,"area":null,"area_key":"any","status":"validated","relationship":null,"text":"Not calculated: rainfall-anomaly differences, because no official rainfall-amount anomaly product was found in the checked ICPAC and EMI products; which forecast is more accurate, because that needs observations and a separate verification design (see Verification); same-event probability differences, because the target windows or spatial supports differ and ICPAC publishes only favoured-category intervals.","evidence_ids":[]}],"evidence":{"platform_forecast_fmam":{"label":"Platform FMAM 2026 forecast data (NetCDF)","kind":"platform","links":[{"label":"Platform map","href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YonSci/calibrated_seasonal_rainfall/b7a480ae214b3431bf96481f4feb23364b596a86/site/assets/maps/fmam2026feb/forecast/FMAM/{view}/tercile_outlook.png"},{"label":"Platform data (NetCDF)","href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YonSci/calibrated_seasonal_rainfall/b7a480ae214b3431bf96481f4feb23364b596a86/site/downloads/data/fmam2026feb/FMAM_forecast_2026.nc"}]},"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_map":{"label":"ICPAC figure: Rainfall forecast - March - May 2026 - IGAD Region","kind":"official_figure","links":[{"label":"Official figure","href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YonSci/calibrated_seasonal_rainfall/b7a480ae214b3431bf96481f4feb23364b596a86/site/assets/external/fmam2026feb/icpac_mam_2026_rainfall.png"},{"label":"Original file","href":"https://www.icpac.net/media/images/GHA-MAM-Rainfall.original.png"}]},"icpac_mam_2026_rainfall_record":{"label":"ICPAC source record","kind":"source_record","links":[{"label":"Source record","href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YonSci/calibrated_seasonal_rainfall/b7a480ae214b3431bf96481f4feb23364b596a86/site/downloads/fmam2026feb_comparison_sources.json"}]},"emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22":{"label":"EMI figure: Bega 2025-26 Assessment and Belg2026 hydro met Bulletin, PDF page 22","kind":"official_figure","links":[{"label":"Official figure","href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YonSci/calibrated_seasonal_rainfall/b7a480ae214b3431bf96481f4feb23364b596a86/site/assets/external/fmam2026feb/emi_belg_2026_outlook_page22_figure.jpg"},{"label":"Original PDF page","href":"https://www.ethiom